# Environment Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5041
@apiPath = /api/game
@contentType = application/json
@accept = application/json

### Create Match with the SAME rule
# Rules are optional. The rules chosen by the creator are inherited by whoever joins the
# waiting match and are returned by GET /match/{id}, GET /matches/waiting and the SignalR
# MatchJoined/MatchStatus payloads as `rules: ["Same"]`.
# With SAME on (FF8 semantics), a tie with one of your own cards counts toward the two-or-more
# ties the rule needs, but own cards can never be captured — only the tied opponent cards flip.
# When SAME and PLUS would both flip the same card, SAME is the reported cause: `triggeredRules`
# comes back ordered SAME first (see the SAME + PLUS sample below).
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["Same"]
}

###

### Create Match with the PLUS rule
# PLUS is independent of SAME: it fires when two or more collisions share the same touching-value
# sum (attack + defense), ignoring the rank comparison — so it can flip a neighbour that beats the
# played card on that side. Own cards may form a matching sum but are never flipped.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["Plus"]
}

###

### Create Match with SAME + PLUS
# Both rules are evaluated on their own; when they overlap on a card, SAME is its cause and
# `triggeredRules` is ["Same","Plus"].
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["Same", "Plus"]
}

###

### Create Match with SAME WALL
# SAME WALL is an independent rule: the board's outer wall counts as an A (10) card for SAME, so a wall
# tie (played card's value on that side is A) counts toward the two-or-more ties the rule needs. It works
# with SAME disabled, and because a wall has no owner it can never be captured — at least one tied
# neighbour still has to be the opponent's.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["SameWall"]
}

###

### Create Match with PLUS WALL
# The wall is an A card for the PLUS grouping too, so a wall contributes the sum `played value + 10` and
# can be one of the two members of a matching sum — which lets PLUS WALL flip a neighbour that beats the
# played card on that side. Works with PLUS disabled.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["PlusWall"]
}

###

### Create Match with every rule
# Rules are independent: a match can enable any subset, and `rules` comes back in enum declaration order
# (Same, Plus, SameWall, PlusWall) — which is also the order `triggeredRules` uses.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["Same", "Plus", "SameWall", "PlusWall"]
}

###

### Create Match without rules (baseline behaviour)
# No rules enabled: ties in a collision never capture anything.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null
}

###

### Create Match with an unknown rule -> 400
# Any name that is not a rule is rejected; the response lists the supported names, which now include
# `Same`, `Plus`, `SameWall` and `PlusWall`. (`Combo` is still unimplemented — swap it for the next real
# rule when it lands.)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["Combo"]
}

###

### Create Match with "None" -> 400
# There is no "none" rule: an empty rules array (or omitting the field) means no rules at all.
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "opponentId": null,
  "rules": ["None"]
}

###

### Inspect the rules enabled on a match
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match/{{testMatchId}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

###

### Play a card (response carries `triggeredRules`, e.g. ["Same"], ["Plus"], ["Same","Plus"],
### ["SameWall"] or ["PlusWall"])
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPath}}/match/{{testMatchId}}/play
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}
{{authHeader}}

{
  "cardId": {{testCardId}},
  "x": 1,
  "y": 1
}

###
